1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"phase-4--4b-speaking-comfort","kind":"phase-article","route":"/roadmap/phase-4/4b-speaking-comfort","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/phase-4/4b-speaking-comfort","sourceHash":"888659470936c8cd608257df1386e3a07043a9a3f6bc019619ebf116c5017c2d","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T23:11:54.474Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"4B — Speaking Comfort","zh":"4B——口语舒适度"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"what-youre-doing","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"What You're Doing","zh":"你正在做什么"}},{"id":"segment-0002","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"You can produce the language — your mouth works, you can form sentences, and you can talk about familiar topics on your own. Now it's time to have real conversations with real people.","zh":"你已经能够产出这门语言——嘴巴能正常运作，能够组织句子，也能独自谈论熟悉的话题。现在，是时候和真实的人进行真实的对话了。"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The goal of this sub-phase is not accuracy. It's comfort. You need to be able to get your thoughts out smoothly enough to have a conversation without constantly freezing, searching for words, or falling back to your native language. You'll make mistakes — lots of them. That's fine. You'll fix them later. Right now, the priority is volume: speak as much as possible, as often as possible.","zh":"本子阶段的目标不是准确性，而是舒适度。你需要足够顺畅地表达想法，在对话中不会不断卡住、苦苦寻找词语，或退回使用母语。你会犯很多错误——非常多。这没关系。之后再改正它们。现在的首要任务是增加产出量：尽可能多说，尽可能经常地说。"}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"This is where your hundreds of hours of input really pay off. You'll find that words come to you more easily than you expected, and that many phrases and sentence patterns you've absorbed through immersion start flowing out naturally. The more you speak, the more this happens.","zh":"这正是你数百小时输入真正发挥作用的地方。你会发现，词语比预想中更容易浮现在脑海里，而通过沉浸吸收的大量短语和句型也开始自然地流露出来。你说得越多，这种情况就越明显。"}},{"id":"segment-0005","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Your first conversation will be rough, but your fourth will sound like a different person.","zh":"你的第一次对话可能会很磕绊，但到第四次时，你听起来就会像换了一个人。"}},{"id":"segment-0006","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Watch Ben's video about doing this after 1000 hours of Czech learning to see what the process looks like:","zh":"观看Ben关于学习捷克语1000小时后进行这项练习的视频，了解这一过程是什么样的："}},{"id":"whats-new","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"What's New","zh":"新增内容"}},{"id":"segment-0008","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Speaking with a partner</strong> — Real conversations with real people. This can be a tutor, a language exchange partner, a friend, or anyone willing to talk with you. Aim for 2-3 conversation sessions per week, at least 30-45 minutes each. The more you speak, the faster you improve. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/speaking-with-partner\">Speaking with Partner</a>","zh":"<strong>与搭档练习口语</strong>——与真实的人进行真实的对话。搭档可以是导师、语言交换伙伴、朋友，或任何愿意和你交谈的人。目标是每周进行2—3次对话，每次至少30—45分钟。你说得越多，进步就越快。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/speaking-with-partner\">与搭档练习口语</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Continue chorusing and monologuing</strong> — On days when you don't have a conversation partner, fill your output time with solo practice: chorusing to refine pronunciation and rhythm, reading aloud for articulation, and monologuing to practice retrieving words under pressure.","zh":"<strong>继续进行跟读和独白练习</strong>——没有对话搭档的日子里，用个人练习填满输出时间：通过跟读优化发音和节奏，通过朗读练习发音，通过独白练习在压力下提取词语。"}},{"id":"segment-0010","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Corrected Reading Aloud (optional)</strong> — Reading aloud with feedback from a tutor or tool that helps you catch pronunciation errors. This is more targeted than uncorrected reading aloud and helps you identify specific sounds or patterns you're getting wrong. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/corrected-reading-aloud\">Corrected Reading Aloud</a>","zh":"<strong>纠正性朗读（可选）</strong>——在导师或工具的反馈下朗读，帮助你发现发音错误。这比未经纠正的朗读更有针对性，能帮助你识别自己读错的具体音素或模式。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/corrected-reading-aloud\">纠正性朗读</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0011","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Don't abandon input.</strong> It's tempting to shift entirely to speaking practice, but you still need substantial input. Your listening and reading continue to feed your acquisition, and stopping input would slow your speaking improvement too. Keep freeflow listening in your daily routine.","zh":"<strong>不要放弃输入。</strong>你可能会想把重点完全转向口语练习，但仍然需要大量输入。听力和阅读会继续为你的语言习得提供养分，停止输入也会拖慢口语进步。继续把自由流听力纳入日常安排。"}},{"id":"your-routine","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Your Routine","zh":"你的日常安排"}},{"id":"segment-0013","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Output becomes the largest block: <a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-pillars-of-language-learning\">The Pillars of Language Learning</a>","zh":"输出成为占比最大的部分：<a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-pillars-of-language-learning\">语言学习的支柱</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0014","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"<strong>Priming:</strong> 10%","zh":"<strong>预热：</strong>10%"},{"en":"<strong>Interactive Immersion:</strong> 20%","zh":"<strong>互动式沉浸：</strong>20%"},{"en":"<strong>Freeflow Immersion:</strong> 30%","zh":"<strong>自由流沉浸：</strong>30%"},{"en":"<strong>Output:</strong> 40%","zh":"<strong>输出：</strong>40%"}]},{"id":"sample-daily-schedule","type":"heading","level":3,"content":{"en":"Sample Daily Schedule","zh":"每日安排示例"}},{"id":"segment-0016","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Vocab study: 10 mins","zh":"词汇学习：10分钟"},{"en":"Interactive Reading/Listening: 20 mins","zh":"互动式阅读/听力：20分钟"},{"en":"Freeflow Listening: 30 mins","zh":"自由流听力：30分钟"},{"en":"Conversation session (3x weekly): 40 mins","zh":"对话练习（每周3次）：40分钟"},{"en":"Non-conversation days — Chorusing, Reading Aloud, Monologuing: 40 mins total","zh":"非对话日——跟读、朗读、独白：共40分钟"}]},{"id":"when-to-move-on","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"When to Move On","zh":"何时进入下一阶段"}},{"id":"segment-0018","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Move to Phase 5 (or the optional Situational Speaking sub-phase) when you:","zh":"满足以下条件后进入第5阶段（或可选的情境口语子阶段）："}},{"id":"segment-0019","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Feel comfortable having a 45-minute conversation without relying on a dictionary","zh":"能够舒适地进行45分钟对话，无需依赖词典"},{"en":"Feel comfortable with the pronunciation and prosody (rhythm and intonation) of the language","zh":"对这门语言的发音和韵律（节奏与语调）感到自然舒适"},{"en":"Can express most of what you want to say, even if imperfectly","zh":"能够表达大部分想说的内容，即使还不够完美"}]},{"id":"research-and-reasoning","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Research and Reasoning","zh":"研究与依据"}},{"id":"segment-0021","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The emphasis on volume during this phase reflects the principle that learners improve most through sustained practice and exposure. Production practice activates the knowledge built through input, allowing learners to test hypotheses about how the language works and to develop the automatic retrieval and speech planning skills necessary for fluent production. <a href=\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-92210-7_6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Swain (1985)</a> characterized this as \"learning by doing\" — the act of producing the language under communicative pressure provides unique feedback (both internal and from the listener) that shapes interlanguage development in ways that input alone cannot.","zh":"本阶段强调产出量，体现了学习者通过持续练习和接触能够获得最大进步这一原则。产出练习会激活通过输入建立的知识，让学习者检验自己对语言运作方式的假设，并培养流畅产出所需的自动化提取和言语规划能力。<a href=\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-92210-7_6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Swain（1985）</a>将其概括为“在实践中学习”——在交流压力下产出语言这一行为，会提供独特的反馈（包括内部反馈和听者反馈），以塑造中介语的发展，而这些效果仅靠输入无法实现。"}}],"cards":[]}}]
